# design/.gitignore — Open Design daemon residue.
#
# This file lives at design/, ONE LEVEL ABOVE the agent's working directory
# (design/mockups/). That placement is deliberate: the design agent runs with
# --permission-mode bypassPermissions, so rules kept inside its cwd could be
# rewritten as an ordinary in-scope edit. From here, the same rewrite requires
# leaving project scope — a loud, reviewable event rather than a silent one.
#
# RULE: ignore machine-local regenerable residue; COMMIT agent-produced content.
# Anything not listed below stays visible in `git status` ON PURPOSE — an
# unrecognized file should surface for investigation, not disappear.
#
# NOTE ON FORMAT: gitignore has NO inline comments — a `#` only starts a comment
# at the start of a line. Every reason below therefore sits ABOVE its pattern.
# (An earlier draft used trailing comments and silently matched nothing; the
# patterns were literally "<pattern>   # reason". Verified with `git check-ignore -v`.)
#
# Citations are into the Open Design source clone @ f52fda2.

# ── confirmed to land in the project folder ──────────────────────────────────

# Per-turn staging copy of the active skill, replaced wholesale every call
# (cwd-aliases.ts). Build-cache class — reproducible from the app's own install.
.od-skills/

# finalize-design flow lock; operators remove it by hand (finalize-design.ts).
.finalize.lock

# finalize's atomic-write temp file (finalize-design.ts).
DESIGN.md.tmp.*

# App-side rename temp (projects.ts).
.od-rename-*.tmp

# ── lands in the package dir (design/xtty-design-system/) ─────────────────────────

# Revision-accept staging; removed in a finally block, but survives a crash.
.tmp-revision-accept-*/

# Scaffold fingerprint. Should NEVER appear for an agent-managed package — its
# presence means artifactMode was lost and the app is about to scaffold over our
# authored files. Ignored because its BODY is review noise, but its EXISTENCE is
# the signal — and `git status` is now blind to it. So design/README.md's
# post-run checklist tests for it explicitly, and scripts/design-link.sh warns
# on it every run. Do not remove that test on the assumption git will show it.
.od-generated.json

# ── defensive ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These resolve app-side today, but this exact bare-project-dir bug class has
# shipped before, so the insurance is free.

.live-artifacts/
.file-versions/
.transcript.jsonl
.transcript.lock
.od-prompt-*.md

# ── DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED — tripwires. Investigate, don't delete blindly ───
#
#   *-v2.html, *-v3.html    Agent revision copies. Promote the winner over the
#                           canonical name and delete the rest BEFORE committing.
#                           Ignoring them would let the good revision hide in an
#                           invisible file while `git status` reads clean.
#   brand-spec.md           A brand source was attached and OUTRANKED our tokens.
#   .mcp.json               The daemon misclassified our working directory.
#   code/ plan/ review/     Plugin-atom output; we do not use those flows.
#   mockups/DESIGN.md       A real document if "finalize" ever runs here.
#
# COMMITTED ON PURPOSE: *.html, *.artifact.json (provenance sidecars),
#   index.html, README.md, assets/**, and all of design/xtty-design-system/**.
#
# NEVER name a subfolder any of: build out dist debug target vendor .build
#   .swiftpm .cache coverage node_modules — the app's own ignore list hides
#   them, so a mockup placed in one would be invisible to the tool.
